  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> be three non-zero vectors such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> are non-collinear if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> is collinear with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> is collinear with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mn>0</mn><mo>→</mo></mover></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></math> is equal to"
